The VoxelGI investigation's logic
=================================

The action its story runs (`{run "marchCone"}`), the click handler of its slice insets (`imageClick`), and its
click on the scene, over the octree its code bakes (src/godot/voxelgi/script.rs: `octreeSize`, `leafOf`).

$[Import* std]
$[Import* render_lab_runtime]
$[Import* godot_voxelgi_values]
$[Import* godot_voxelgi_natives]
$[ImportAs rl_runtime rt]

The arguments a story passes to `marchCone` (`run.seconds=…`); the optional ones are options.
$[# MarchCone [% {Struct {'
    {Field "seconds" Float}
    {Field "from" {Option Int}}
    {Field "to" {Option Int}}}}]]

Steps a cone's march (`coneSteps`) from `from` (0 by default) to `to` (16 by default), one sample every `seconds`.
$[# marchCone {: {^ {elapsed run}
    [# seconds {.seconds run}]
    [# from {withDefault {.from run} 0}]
    [# to {withDefault {.to run} 16}]
    {!if {<= seconds 0.0}
        {error f"{a step takes $seconds s; it takes longer than 0}"}
        {' {setConeSteps {float {min {+ from {steps seconds elapsed}} to}}}}}} {Action MarchCone}}]

Picks the cell under a click on a slice inset (x across, z down, at the slice's height; the slice is the leaves'
grid).
$[# pickSliceCell {: {^ {click}
    [# s {octreeSize}]
    [# y {clamp {.y {leafOf {vec3 0.0 {sliceHeight} 0.0}}} 0 {- {.y s} 1}}]
    [# x {clamp {truncate {* {.u click} {float {.x s}}}} 0 {- {.x s} 1}}]
    [# z {clamp {truncate {* {.v click} {float {.z s}}}} 0 {- {.z s} 1}}]
    {' {setCellX {float x}} {setCellY {float y}} {setCellZ {float z}}}} ClickHandler}]

A click on the scene picks the leaf cell of the surface it hits: just behind the point, along the surface's normal.
A click that hits nothing picks nothing.
$[# scene {: {^ {click} {caseOption
    {rt::trace {.u click} {.v click} {'}}
    {^ {} {'}}
    {^ {hit}
        [# c {leafOf {vsub {.point hit} {vscale {.normal hit} 0.01}}}]
        {'
            {setCellX {float {.x c}}}
            {setCellY {float {.y c}}}
            {setCellZ {float {.z c}}}}}}} ClickHandler}]
